  "aiContextParagraph": "Pope Leo XIV has embarked on a 12-day, three-country tour of South America, marking his return to international travel following a recent lung cancer operation. The 71-year-old leader of the Catholic Church began the tour in Uruguay, where he addressed a crowd of over 40,000 people during a celebratory Mass. Following this, he traveled to Argentina, where he was received by President Javier Milei. Throughout the trip, the Pope has engaged with several social issues, including calling for universal healthcare and urging respect for women in the context of the region's femicide crisis. Observers have noted that the Argentine visit is expected to generate significant public turnout. Despite his recent health challenges, officials have characterized the Pope's condition as being in good health as he continues his diplomatic and pastoral itinerary.",
